==Portuguese==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|pt|porq̃}} {{qualifier|obsolete|abbreviation}}
* {{l|pt|pq}} {{qualifier|Internet slang}}
* {{l|pt|perque}} {{qualifier|obsolete}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|roa-opt|pt}} {{m|roa-opt|porque}}, corresponding to {{compound|pt|por|que|t1=for|t2=that}}.

Cognate with {{cog|gl|porque}}, {{cog|es|porque}}, {{cog|ca|perquè}}, {{cog|fr|parce que}} and {{cog|it|perché}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|Portugal}} {{IPA|pt|/ˈpuɾ.kɨ/}}
* {{a|Brazil}} {{IPA|pt|/puʁ.ˈke/}}
** {{a|Caipira}} {{IPA|pt|/puɻ.ˈke/}}
** {{a|South Brazil}} {{IPA|pt|/poɹ.ˈke/|/poɾ.ˈke/}}
* {{hyphenation|pt|por|que}}

===Conjunction===
{{head|pt|conjunction}}

# {{l|en|because}}; {{l|en|for}} {{gloss|''introduces an explanation to the claim in the previous clause''}}
#: {{ux|pt|Aproveita tua vida '''porque''' ela é curta!|Enjoy your life '''because''' it is short!}}

